    {
        "content": "<p>I want to prove the following example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instBEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instBEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">beq</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However in module mode, the definition of <code>Sum.instBEq.beq</code> is not imported and there are no theorem about it (make it an opaque), so this thing become unprovable.</p>\n<p>See linked PR at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14895\">lean4#14895</a>.</p>",
        "id": 618158092,
        "sender_full_name": "Kitsune Kiriha",
        "timestamp": 1787459441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One workaround is to add <code>import all Init.Data.Sum.Basic</code></p>",
        "id": 618162424,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1787463566
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's quite the antipattern though. Is there no API about the equality? A LawfulBEq instance, maybe?</p>",
        "id": 618171937,
        "sender_full_name": "Ruben Van de Velde",
        "timestamp": 1787472320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not any. That's why I propose the <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14895\">PR</a> to give it an LawfulBEq.</p>",
        "id": 618172240,
        "sender_full_name": "Kitsune Kiriha",
        "timestamp": 1787472544
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm reworking deriving handlers including <code>BEq</code> and <code>LawfulBEq</code> right now so it's maybe not the best time to add a manual <code>LawfulBEq</code> instance. I'm thinking of making these exposed by default though so this shouldn't be a problem anymore.</p>",
        "id": 618193625,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1787488605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I pushed a commit to <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/14895\">lean4#14895</a>, it works fine via <code>deriving</code> as long as you do <code>ReflEq</code> along the way.</p>",
        "id": 618236228,
